6. Focus on alignment: As you move through these exercises, pay attention to how your body feels. Notice any areas where you may be compensating for imbalances or misalignments.

7. Listen to your body: Pay attention to any discomfort or pain you may experience during these exercises. This can be a sign that an area of your body needs further attention or care.

8. Regularly practice self-assessment: Make it a habit to regularly check your body's balance and alignment. This can help you identify any potential issues before they become problems and allow you to address them effectively.

